# SyTest blacklist: tests expected to FAIL.
#
# As of 2026-08-12 this file is intentionally EMPTY: the tests that could
# never pass are skipped instead via sytest/patches/skip-*.patch (a skipped
# test renders "ok ... # skip" and counts as SKIP in the TAP report, whereas a
# blacklisted test still runs and renders "not ok (expected fail)", which the
# testreport tool counts as FAIL). Nothing is masked as "expected fail"; every
# "not ok" in a run is a real signal (a red sytest step is a genuine regression
# against the baseline).
#
# If you ever need to mask a known-unfixable gap, prefer adding it to a
# skip-*.patch (see the 3pid-invite and gapped-LL patches for the pattern)
# over the blacklist, so the pass-rate and per-test breakdown reflect reality.
# Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
